// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 2 (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P6): the same LOCAL text pushed twice into a
// LOCAL list of text -- the purely-local shape of the same class C1's
// fixtures cover for globals. Originally (4e): `p6L` (fresh init, only ever
// a push receiver) qualified for a scope-exit element-free loop, but that
// loop would free `p6X`'s handle twice, once per element slot: SIGSEGV at
// handler scope exit. The fix (`lowEscapeWalkMethodCall`: a push/add/
// unshift value that fails `lowEscapeFreshInit` disqualifies the receiver
// too) disqualifies `p6L`'s DEEP release the first time `p6X` -- a bare
// identifier, never fresh -- is pushed; still true today (container
// elements are Task 5's still-unmigrated slot class, untouched by ARC Task
// 4 -- push never retains, so a deep element-walk here would still
// double-free the one handle both push sites share).
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores + unconditional local release):
// `p6X` itself is ALSO disqualified, but for a DIFFERENT, still-genuinely-
// unsafe reason (`lowFreeUnsafe`, not just `lowFreeDisq`): it was handed to
// a push argument, a consumer this task's migration doesn't cover (see
// `lowStoreIsBirth`'s own doc comment on `lowEscapeWalkArgsHandoff`) -- so
// unlike most disqualified locals, `p6X` is SKIPPED entirely at scope exit,
// not shallow-released (confirmed against the emitted C: no
// `rt_text_release(cv_p6X)` anywhere). `p6L`'s own list handle, by
// contrast, IS a real named-slot local now covered by unconditional
// release -- it gets a genuine shallow release at scope exit (deep stays
// gated on the same unmigrated-elements proof as before -- confirmed
// against the emitted C: bare `rt_list_release(cv_p6L)`, no element loop).
// Expected strict-mode leak count: 2 (see ../p6_dup_push_local.leaks,
// dropped from 4) -- `p6X`'s text only (struct box + data handle, 2
// blocks; the one handle both push sites share, still never freed). Not a
// bug -- container-element ownership is explicitly out of this task's
// scope, staged for Task 5.

func runP6DupPushLocal() {
    var p6L: list of text
    var p6X: text = "dup"
    p6L.push(p6X)
    p6L.push(p6X)
    alert("p6 done")
}
